  },
  "format": "Each case: zoneFor(type, id, fields) for a record written in writtenIn (Library for the personal library, or Space-<spaceID>) = expect, a zone name. replica is what the client holds: zone name → record type → id → the record's fields as placement reads them (a Notebook's redirect fields mergedInto, movedTo and movingTo; a ZoneRoot's kind and primaryID; {} otherwise). Each type's rule is its home in schema/cloudkit-schema.json (homeRules). In order: a type with a spaceRule whose field value is not allowed (or absent) is Library; an id starting with one of home.personalIDPrefixes is Library; a record whose id is the primaryID of a held space root of kind home.primaryOfSpace is that space. Then by rule: library → Library; current → writtenIn when it is a space, else privateZone; parent → the zone of the parent named by fields[field] (its type is parent, or parents[fields[kindField]]; an unknown kind gives the current rule with Library): a priv-only parent type is Library; otherwise the zones holding that parent id are taken in the order writtenIn (when a space), then Library or Catalog, then the first space by name; a Notebook parent is then resolved from there (resolve.json) and, when the notebook it reaches shows movingTo S and the replica holds the same id in Space-S, it is Space-S; a parent not held, or an empty field, gives the zone a new record of the parent type would get (its own home applied with nothing known); owner → privateZone for a personal role (fields[roleField]); the owner type fields[typeField] unknown → the current rule with privateZone; else the owner's zone by the parent rule, kept when it is a space, privateZone otherwise.",
  "status": "Written with WP2 from the home rules; built by scripts/schema/build-vectors.mjs, whose reference placement is independent of both sync cores.",
